 "method": "Zero-paid reconstruction of each memory-on paid prompt's served set (Codex CP4 review 21, ruling 6), from the archived store\n(evidence/store-archive, read-only; no Redis, no Docker): the AOF's commands in order, each stream entry's id being its\ntransaction time. Writes evidence/served-reconstruction.json; make_paid_attempts.py reads it for R2 and R4's serving half.\n\nWhat a turn is served (src/optimus/context/memory_serving.py `from_store` at every paid head, checked below): the project's\nitems whose latest confirmed version is servable (trust not off, status active, `context_engine.memory_projection`) and has a\nstatement, minus branch-limited items on another branch and items whose pinned file changed (both come from the item's\nlineage), then at most 50 user items and 3 agent lessons. For a prompt, the served set is derived only when the inputs fix it:\n- the confirmed view is known: every event at or before the window's start is confirmed there (a `durable` watermark at or\n  past it);\n- no item event falls inside the window, so the read time within it cannot matter;\n- every servable item's lineage has no branch limit and no file pin, so no workspace or branch state is needed;\n- no agent lesson exists and at most 50 user items do, so no ranking or limit applies.\nOtherwise the prompt is UNKNOWN, with the input that is missing.",
